t(11, 1790, """Every father who marries off his son, because his son may be blessed with a child, should read this post

When Muhammad Ali DELIBERATELY knocked himself down before this child, he did not fall because the child was strong and stronger than him! Muhammad Ali knocked himself down by a knockout blow at the hand of a small child, because the child in the world:
⭕⭕ is the man of the future, who must be given very high self-confidence, and not be trampled as millions who have had children do in our bad time .. "Father" is a word the size of a continent; in every million there are perhaps 1000 fathers, but in every million there are a million begetters!

And because the child
⭕⭕ is the hope of the Ummah in its coming tomorrow, and the one who completes, by the power of Allah the Exalted, the human mission built on the divine charge to humanity!

Muhammad Ali DELIBERATELY knocked himself down to send a message to the world .. to alert millions of fathers around the world to the reality of the jewel and precious diamond in their hands, which is "the children".

If you, as a father, do not DELIBERATELY knock yourself to the ground for your son, with wisdom, correctness and sound educational planning, you will never be a father, but will remain a begetter .. and the difference between father and begetter is a huge difference, like that between heaven and earth!

Our children are more precious than us .. a sentence the father will understand, and a sentence the begetter will not understand however long he lives!""")

t(12, 115, """The mistakes that happen when the father lives as a father and not a begetter, and still meets ingratitude, those mistakes are what give the wrong results.

The mistake is mostly the absence of balance in the father's relationship with his children! Being a father is what the religion commanded, but a balanced father; fatherhood must never make you burn like a candle; that is not fatherhood, that is "an absence of wisdom"!

🔴 The begetter feeds, nourishes, beats, drags, tramples, breaks the spirit, is frightening and terrifying; the ego kills him outright, and every idea deviating from religion drags him along
🟢 And the father feeds, nourishes, refines, is wise, calm, sincerely loving, merciful, forgiving, a teacher lighting up the way, respectful of his son's human dignity, stopping at the commands of the Book and the Sunnah.

As for the detail of the meaning of the word "ab (father)" in the Book of our Mighty Lord:
The word is used in the station of advice, guidance, responsibility and example, and the word "ab" came, not "walid"! The word "ab" in the Book of our Lord indicates (care, upbringing and walking the right path). Of this is the saying of our Mighty Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, exalted be He greatly:
"The religion of your father Ibrahim": its use for the grandfather whose religion guides us
And also its use for the uncle, described as a father, the one whose conduct on the straight Lordly path guides us: "We will worship your God and the God of your fathers Ibrahim, Isma'il and Ishaq" (Isma'il was Ya'qub's uncle).

As for kindness and good treatment, it came in our Mighty Lord's direction for the walidayn, for their right to good treatment, even if they did not fulfil the great role of fatherhood and motherhood and only fulfilled the role of birth and feeding.""")

